    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `initials` field to the owner GET response, computed as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo edits, each in the layer that owns the concern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, alongside the existing derived `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the mapper already owns derived presentation fields (`displayName`), so `initials` lives there too. I added a `@Mapping` targeting `initials` via `initials(owner)`, a small `default` method that composes a private `firstInitial(String)` helper (`Character.toUpperCase(name.charAt(0)) + \".\"`) for each name \u2014 no duplicated logic, single responsibility. `charAt(0)` is safe because both names are `required` with `minLength: 1` in the schema.\n\nThe presentation-layer computation follows the exact pattern already established for `displayName`, keeping the entity and the endpoint pipeline untouched.",
